VeridianOS: no moc includes where there is nothing to moc

The screen locker KCM's kscreenlockerdata.cpp includes its ".moc" file,
but contains no Q_OBJECT, Q_GADGET, Q_NAMESPACE or K_PLUGIN_* (its
QObject classes are declared in headers, which AutoMoc handles on its
own), so AutoMoc generated nothing for it and warned
("includes the moc file ..., but does not contain a Q_OBJECT ...").
The include is removed.

--- a/kcm/kscreenlockerdata.cpp
+++ b/kcm/kscreenlockerdata.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,4 @@
     return KScreenSaverSettings::getInstance().isDefaults() && m_appearanceSettings->isDefaults();
 }
 
-#include "kscreenlockerdata.moc"
-
 #include "moc_kscreenlockerdata.cpp"
